            "relation": "PRODUCES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "convective available potential energy",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "To address the central research question of how anthropogenic warming alters the intensity of storm Gloria, we need to firstly, reproduce the synoptic-scale dynamics of the event correctly and secondly, ensure that the warming scenarios used in the comparison are representative of the back- ground climates they intend to emulate. To answer the second point, we thereforeexamine the 7-year DJF distributions (2017 excluded as a spin-up) of four key variables in the ES region: precipitable water (PW), integrated vapor transport (IVT), convective available potential energy (CAPE) and precipitation, all of which contributed to the extremeness of storm Gloria.",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
